# Same torch pin as the hardware-proven kimodo, motionbricks and moss-vl-realtime recipes: the
# creator's torch 2.5.1 has no GB10 (aarch64, CUDA 13) build, so this is a platform fact, not a
# creator choice; hymotion uses plain torch APIs (SDPA attention, flash-attn is optional).
torch==2.14.0+cu130
# The creator's pins (requirements.txt at c71ea6c6) where they resolve on Python 3.12 aarch64.
# numpy below 2; transformers 4.53.3 (Qwen3 needs at least 4.51) with the huggingface-hub it
# accepts (below 1.0); accelerate is what low_cpu_mem_usage=True in the creator's text encoder needs.
numpy==1.26.4
scipy==1.15.3
transformers==4.53.3
huggingface-hub==0.30.0
accelerate==0.30.1
safetensors==0.5.3
einops==0.8.1
torchdiffeq==0.2.5
# The creator pins 6.0, which has no Python 3.12 wheel and does not build; 6.0.2 reads the same config.yml.
PyYAML==6.0.2
requests==2.32.4
# hymotion/utils/t2m_runtime.py imports prompt_rewrite, which imports openai at module level
# even when the prompt rewriter is disabled; no request is ever made to it.
openai==1.78.1
# Not installed, on purpose: fbxsdkpy (the Autodesk FBX SDK has no aarch64 build; the BVH is written by
